{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Mocked me.</b> An unusual word, because the tav is raphe (without dagesh), for its root is with dagesh, as in וַיְהַתַּל בהם אליהו (1 Kings 18:27), in the manner of mockery:" "<b>Ten times.</b> From the root of מְנֵה את העם (2 Samuel 24:1), and the meaning is ten in number, or he mentioned ten because it is the sum of counting:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra notes that the tav in התל is lenited (raphe) rather than fortified (with dagesh) as in the root form cited from 1 Kings.", 1 "Rendered מונים from the root מנה 'to count,' as Ibn Ezra's cited parallel confirms."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:33.391229045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}